4255   1740             
4256   1740             ; Per-tile hit-window + X-offset table for in-formation aliens:
4257   1740             ; Lookup table used in the player-bullet vs. alien collision routine `L0E10`,
4258   1740             ; specifically for aliens that are still sitting in the base formation.
4259   1740             ; Indexed by the alien tile's character type.
4260   1740             ; How the index is formed:
4261   1740             ; In `L0E10`, the code reads the character drawn under the bullet.
4262   1740             ; After rejecting explosion parts (`≥$C0`), empty cells (`<$60`), and out-of-formation aliens (`≥$68` -> handled by `L0E39`),
4263   1740             ; it's left with in-formation foreground tiles `$60`–`$67`.
4264   1740             ; Meaning of the 4 bytes:
4265   1740             ; Byte 0 — upper bound of the horizontal hit window (`$0E31`): `bulletX & 7` must be < byte 0, else `RET NC` (miss).
4266   1740             ; Byte 1 — lower bound of the hit window (`$0E34`): `bulletX & 7` must be >= byte 1, else `RET C` (miss).
4267   1740             ;          So bytes 0/1 define the `[byte1, byte0)` pixel-column range inside that 8-pixel tile where the alien graphic is actually solid.
4268   1740             ;          (E.g. type 0 = full width `[0,8)`; type 1 = only column 0; type 2 = columns `[1,8)`.)
4269   1740             ; Byte 2 — signed X correction (`$0E70`/`L0E70`): added to the bullet's cell-aligned X to reconstruct the screen X of the hit target,
4270   1740             ;          which is then used to locate the matching alien object in the alien control table at `M4B70`.
4271   1740             ;          Because a formation alien is drawn from several tiles, byte 2 shifts the coordinate from the tile that was hit
4272   1740             ;          back to the alien's anchor X, so the correct alien object is found and killed.
4273   1740             ; Byte 3 — `$FF`, unused padding.
4274   1740             T1740:
4275   1740 08 00 00 FF                        .DB $08, $00, $00, $FF, $01, $00, $F8, $FF, $08, $01, $02, $FF, $04, $00, $FA, $FF ;
4275   1744 01 00 F8 FF 
4275   1748 08 01 02 FF 
4275   174C 04 00 FA FF 
4276   1750 08 01 04 FF                        .DB $08, $01, $04, $FF, $08, $00, $FC, $FF, $08, $05, $06, $FF, $08, $00, $FE, $FF ;
4276   1754 08 00 FC FF 
4276   1758 08 05 06 FF 
4276   175C 08 00 FE FF 
