4463   1B40             ; Character block shapes table using setB.
4464   1B40             ; Parts of the mothership's purple conveyor belt.
4465   1B40             ; So an ordinary belt hit:
4466   1B40             ; 1. Consumes the bullet (`AND $F7`).
4467   1B40             ; 2. Sets the "mother-ship hit" flag `$4366` -> plays the hit sound; no score is awarded.
4468   1B40             ; 3. Swaps the hit tile for a "damaged" belt tile from `T1B40/T1B48/T1B50`,
4469   1B40             ;    chosen by the bullet's X position (left/right half) and the tile's low nibble
4470   1B40             ;     — so the belt visibly chips/breaks apart where you shoot it.
4471   1B40             T1B40:
4472   1B40 6C                                 .DB $6C
4473   1B41 6D                                 .DB $6D
4474   1B42 6E                                 .DB $6E
4475   1B43 6F                                 .DB $6F
