5264   22FA             ;*****************************************************************************
5265   22FA             ;* Rotate the conveyor belt:
5266   22FA             ;* How the "rotation" actually works:
5267   22FA             ;* Each belt tile is a code in `$60`–`$6F`, i.e. `$60 + p` where `p` is a 4-bit phase (0–15)
5268   22FA             ;* that selects which frame of the belt-link graphic is shown. The routine treats that 4-bit phase as two 2-bit halves.
5269   22FA             ;* - high half = bits 2–3
5270   22FA             ;* - low half = bits 0–1
5271   22FA             ;* Walking up the belt column (`L -= $20` each step), every tile is rebuilt as:
5272   22FA             ;* new_phase = (previous_tile.low2 << 2) | (current_tile.high2)
5273   22FA             ;* new_tile  = $60 | new_phase
5274   22FA             ;* In other words:
5275   22FA             ;* - a tile's new high 2 bits come from the lower neighbour's old low 2 bits, and
5276   22FA             ;* - its new low 2 bits come from its own old high 2 bits.
5277   22FA             ;* That is a 2-bit-per-tile shift register running up the column:
5278   22FA             ;* Every animation step, the belt-link pattern marches exactly one 2-bit field up the chain.
5279   22FA             ;* The seed value read from `$488A` feeds a fresh pattern into the bottom of the chain each step,
5280   22FA             ;* so the motion is continuous and never runs out of pattern.
5281   22FA             ;* Because the cumulative effect is "every belt segment's pattern shifts one position along the belt each tick",
5282   22FA             ;* the row of `$60`–`$6F` tiles cycles through their link graphics in lock-step — which the eye reads as the belt rotating/conveying.
5283   22FA             ;*****************************************************************************
5284   22FA             L22FA:
5285   22FA 21 AA 4A                           LD      HL,BackgroundScreen+$2AA
5286   22FD 06 12                              LD      B,$12               
5287   22FF 3A 8A 48                           LD      A,(BackgroundScreen+$8A)
5288   2302 4F                                 LD      C,A                 
5289   2303             L2303:
5290   2303 79                                 LD      A,C                 
5291   2304 E6 03                              AND     $03                 
5292   2306 07                                 RLCA                        ; Multiply by 4 ..
5293   2307 07                                 RLCA                        ; ..
5294   2308 57                                 LD      D,A                 
5295   2309 4E                                 LD      C,(HL)              
5296   230A 79                                 LD      A,C                 
5297   230B E6 0C                              AND     $0C                 
5298   230D 0F                                 RRCA                        
5299   230E 0F                                 RRCA                        
5300   230F B2                                 OR      D                   
5301   2310 F6 60                              OR      $60                 
5302   2312 77                                 LD      (HL),A              
5303   2313 7D                                 LD      A,L                 
5304   2314 D6 20                              SUB     $20                 
5305   2316 6F                                 LD      L,A                 
5306   2317 D2 1B 23                           JP      NC,L231B            ; 
5307   231A 25                                 DEC     H                   
5308   231B             L231B:
5309   231B 05                                 DEC     B                   
5310   231C C2 03 23                           JP      NZ,L2303            ; 
5311   231F C9                                 RET                         
5312   2320             
5313   2322                                    .ORG $2322
5314   2322             ;*****************************************************************************
5315   2322             ;* Animation of the mothership's antenna and the alien pilot.
5316   2322             ;*****************************************************************************
5317   2322             L2322:
5318   2322 21 A7 43                           LD      HL,AnimationCounter ; 
5319   2325 34                                 INC     (HL)                ; increment the animation counter
5320   2326 7E                                 LD      A,(HL)              ;
5321   2327 E6 07                              AND     $07                 ; mask out 0000_0111, in order to count from 0 to 7 for 8 frames
5322   2329 07                                 RLCA                        ; Multiply by 8 ..
5323   232A 07                                 RLCA                        ; ..to get..
5324   232B 07                                 RLCA                        ; ..the frame data adress (8 characters per frame)
5325   232C C6 C0                              ADD     T1BC0 & $FF         ; LSB of T1BC0
5326   232E 6F                                 LD      L,A                 ;
5327   232F 26 1B                              LD      H,T1BC0 >> 8        ; MSB of T1BC0
5328   2331 11 A6 49                           LD      DE,BackgroundScreen+$1A6; at the middle of the mothership
5329   2334 01 02 04                           LD      BC,$0402            ; images are 2x4
5330   2337 C3 D6 0A                           JP      DrawImageCbyB       ; 
5331   233A             ; Intro-splash bird animation script table:
5332   233A             ; A list of bird shape indices that, played in order, make the attract-mode bird grow
5333   233A             ; from a twinkling star into a full flapping Phoenix and then shrink back.
5334   233A             ; Used at `DrawIntroBirdAnimationFrame` (`$21DC`).
5335   233A             ; The mapping is a two-level lookup:
5336   233A             ; M4399  --(>>3)-->  T233A[i] = shape index
5337   233A             ;                      |
5338   233A             ;                      +--(*8)--+--(+ M4399&7 phase)--> T3E08 entry --> bird tile-block address
5339   233A             ; So `T233A` is essentially a tiny animation timeline.
5340   233A             ; The index `M4399 >> 3` walks through it, each step lasting 8 ticks (during which `M4399 & 7` animates the wings),
5341   233A             ; turning the abstract growth/flap/shrink choreography into concrete shape indices that `DrawBirdObject` renders.
5342   233A             ; The trailing `FF` signals the end of the script (it's the sentinel the surrounding intro logic uses to know the sequence is finished).
5343   233A             T233A:
5344   233A 01 02 03 04                        .DB $01, $02, $03, $04, $05, $06, $07, $0A, $07, $0A, $07, $0A, $07, $0A, $07, $0A
5344   233E 05 06 07 0A 
5344   2342 07 0A 07 0A 
5344   2346 07 0A 07 0A 
5345   234A 09 08 04 03                        .DB $09, $08, $04, $03, $02, $01, $FF
5345   234E 02 01 FF 
5346   2351             
5347   2351             ;*****************************************************************************
5348   2351             ;* Mother-ship collision routine:
5349   2351             ;* During the mother-ship levels (game level ≥ 8), `L2000` -> `L24A0` calls `L2351`.
5350   2351             ;* It looks up the tile at the (scroll-adjusted) bullet position 
5351   2351             ;* and explicitly tests for the `$4C`–`$4F` group.
5352   2351             ;*****************************************************************************
5353   2351             L2351:
5354   2351 1A                                 LD      A,(DE)              
5355   2352 E6 08                              AND     $08                 
5356   2354 C8                                 RET     Z                   
5357   2355 7E                                 LD      A,(HL)              
5358   2356 2C                                 INC     L                   
5359   2357 6E                                 LD      L,(HL)              
5360   2358 C6 08                              ADD     $08                 
5361   235A 67                                 LD      H,A                 
5362   235B 3A B9 43                           LD      A,(CounterB9)       ; 
5363   235E 0F                                 RRCA                        
5364   235F 0F                                 RRCA                        
5365   2360 0F                                 RRCA                        
5366   2361 85                                 ADD     A,L                 
5367   2362 E6 1F                              AND     $1F                 
5368   2364 47                                 LD      B,A                 
5369   2365 7D                                 LD      A,L                 
5370   2366 E6 E0                              AND     $E0                 
5371   2368 B0                                 OR      B                   
5372   2369 6F                                 LD      L,A                 
5373   236A 7E                                 LD      A,(HL)              
5374   236B 47                                 LD      B,A                 
5375   236C E6 FC                              AND     $FC                 
5376   236E FE 4C                              CP      $4C                 
5377   2370 CA 7B 23                           JP      Z,L237B             ; 
5378   2373 E6 F0                              AND     $F0                 
5379   2375 FE 60                              CP      $60                 
5380   2377 CA 98 23                           JP      Z,L2398             ; 
5381   237A C9                                 RET                         
5382   237B             ;*****************************************************************************
5383   237B             ;* The mothership's protective shield was hit by a player bullet.
5384   237B             ;* Shield erosion.
5385   237B             ;* So a hit on a `$4C`–`$4F` tile does the following, with no score awarded:
5386   237B             ;* 1. The bullet is consumed (`AND $F7` clears the active bit) — the shot stops there; it does not punch through.
5387   237B             ;* 2. A "mother-ship hit" is registered (`$4366 = $FF`), which drives the hit sound effect.
5388   237B             ;* 3. The tile is decremented one step: `$4F -> $4E -> $4D -> $4C -> $4B`.
5389   237B             ;*    Because the four tiles are an increasing-density gradient, each shot visually "chips" the curved armour one notch thinner.
5390   237B             ;* 4. When a tile erodes to `$4B` it's cleared to `$00` (that chunk of shield is gone).
5391   237B             ;*    If the tile behind it is the solid hull `$5E`, that hull tile is turned into a fresh `$4F`,
5392   237B             ;*    i.e. the next layer of hull becomes the new erodible shield edge.
5393   237B             ;*****************************************************************************
5394   237B             L237B:
5395   237B 1A                                 LD      A,(DE)              
5396   237C E6 F7                              AND     $F7                 
5397   237E 12                                 LD      (DE),A              
5398   237F 3E FF                              LD      A,$FF               
5399   2381 32 66 43                           LD      (M4366),A           ; 
5400   2384 78                                 LD      A,B                 
5401   2385 3D                                 DEC     A                   
5402   2386 77                                 LD      (HL),A              
5403   2387 FE 4B                              CP      $4B                 
5404   2389 C0                                 RET     NZ                  
5405   238A 36 00                              LD      (HL),$00            
5406   238C 2D                                 DEC     L                   
5407   238D 7E                                 LD      A,(HL)              
5408   238E FE 5E                              CP      $5E                 
5409   2390 C0                                 RET     NZ                  
5410   2391 36 4F                              LD      (HL),$4F            
5411   2393 C9                                 RET                         
5412   2394             
5413   2398                                    .ORG $2398
