8844   3ED0             ; Vertical scrolling/descent motion of the birds attack formation.
8845   3ED0             ; Consumed by the bird vertical-movement routine `L2600` and its helper `L2668`.
8846   3ED0             ; Dithered vertical-scroll increment table:
8847   3ED0             ; Used to generate fractional (sub-pixel) scroll speeds for the formation's descent. In `L2600`.
8848   3ED0             ; - The index is `row + column`, where the *row* (`0/4/8/12`) is the animation-frame parity from `Counter9A+1`,
8849   3ED0             ;   and the column (`0–3`) is the descent sub-phase `B4BD5 & 3`.
8850   3ED0             ; - The value (only ever `0` or `1`) is added to the coarse speed `(B4BD5>>2)&7`
8851   3ED0             ;   to form the per-frame scroll delta, which is then subtracted from `CounterB9` and written to the hardware scroll register `$5800`.
8852   3ED0             ; This lets the game realise non-integer average descent rates (e.g. an effective 3 1/2 px/frame) by alternating between `n` and `n+1` across frames/sub-phases,
8853   3ED0             ; giving smooth variable-speed scrolling. (The alternate path `L2650` reuses the same table but adds to `CounterB9` for the return/upward motion.)
8854   3ED0             T3ED0:
8855   3ED0 01 01 01 01                        .DB $01, $01, $01, $01
8856   3ED4 00 00 01 01                        .DB $00, $00, $01, $01
8857   3ED8 00 01 01 01                        .DB $00, $01, $01, $01
8858   3EDC 00 00 00 01                        .DB $00, $00, $00, $01
8859   3EE0             
8860   3EE0             ; Descent-speed clamp curve table:
8861   3EE0             ; This 32-byte block is indexed by `B4BD6` (a 0–31 value) and acts as a per-position speed limit on the computed descent step in `L2668`.
8862   3EE0             ; `B4BD6` is computed in `L26D0`/`$26EE` as `(B4BD2 + D + E) & $1F` after scanning the live bird objects (`M4BA8…`).
8863   3EE0             ; So it encodes the formation's current vertical scroll phase combined with how many birds remain and where they are.
8864   3EE0             ; The table value caps `B` (a step candidate derived from `M436E`, the wave timer `Counter9A`, and `AliensLeft`),
8865   3EE0             ; and the clamped result becomes `B4BD5` — which is exactly the value Part 1 uses to pick the scroll increment.
8866   3EE0             ; The values trace a speed envelope across the descent: `5->4->3->2->1->0`, a flat `0` hold, 
8867   3EE0             ; then a gradual rise `1->2->...->8` and back to `6`.
8868   3EE0             ; In effect it makes the swooping formation decelerate to a stop, pause, then accelerate again as it moves through the screen.
8869   3EE0             T3EE0:
8870   3EE0 05 04 03 02                        .DB $05, $04, $03, $02, $01, $00
8870   3EE4 01 00 
8871   3EE6 00 00 00 00                        .DB $00, $00, $00, $00, $01, $01
8871   3EEA 01 01 
8872   3EEC 01 01 02 02                        .DB $01, $01, $02, $02
8873   3EF0 02 02 03 03                        .DB $02, $02, $03, $03
8874   3EF4 03 04 04 04                        .DB $03, $04, $04, $04
8875   3EF8 05 05 06 06                        .DB $05, $05, $06, $06
8876   3EFC 07 08 07 06                        .DB $07, $08, $07, $06
